How long after the policy load is /dev/console supposed to
become console_device_t? immediately after policy load the
label of /dev/console is system_u:system_r:kernel_t. I tried to
sleep init for 5 and 30 seconds before spawning the init
scripts the console is still kernel_t. And if i check the
console label using getfattr its console_device_t. I cant boot
at all in enforcing mode because no matter what i do the /dev
node labels are all kernel_t. the scripts are being run as
system_u:system_r:initrc_t.

this is the first avc denied message after the initializations
by simpleinit is finished.

avc: denied { use } for pid=18 exe=/bin/bash path=/dev/console
dev=hda16 ino=17895218 scontext=system_u:system_r:initrc_t
tcontext=system_u:system_r:kernel_t tclass=fd

im using a modified load_policy as init to load the policy file
and exec /sbin/simpleinit. thats the init from util-linux-2.12.
looking at the sysvinit_patches its essentially the same. both
files are labeled system_u:object_r:init_exec_t. sould i
setfilecon the console device before i exec simpleinit?
